+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, typed `TurnUsage`, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- A round whose provider reports no usage is skipped in the total rather than poisoning it ([validated by: totals the rounds that reported usage](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L29)).
+- A turn where no round reported still reports `undefined`, not a zeroed total ([validated by: stays undefined when no round reported](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L39)).
+- The same aggregation reaches `afterModelResponse` itself: a tool-round turn whose provider reports usage on only some rounds delivers the total of the rounds that reported, and a tool-less turn whose provider reports no usage delivers `undefined` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
